# Cloudflare Pages header rules. Pages consumes this file and does not serve it.
#
# Why this exists (2026-07-31): Pages' default is max-age=14400 on every asset,
# while index.html is max-age=0. That combination broke the site for returning
# visitors — new HTML would run up to four hours of stale JS/CSS. It was caught
# after the lightbox rewrite shipped: the markup had the new data-full hooks but
# the cached main.js knew nothing about them, so the Amenities images simply did
# not open. Several "the deploy hasn't propagated" moments the same day were
# this, not edge lag.
#
# Filenames here are stable (no content hashing — there is no build step), so
# the only safe policy for code is to revalidate every load. That costs a 304
# when nothing changed and removes the stale-code window entirely.
#
# Images, fonts and other assets deliberately keep the Pages default: their
# contents never change under a given filename, and a new render ships under a
# new name.

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
